# ex34 — board literal fixture (mirrors demos/6-space/34-board-literal.bqn)
# The glyph lattice comes from the statement's own string literal; the world starts empty.
# pieceOf maps a glyph to its piece proto — here the piece IS the glyph (the .bqn's
# piece ≡ occupied/⥊board), so the lookup wraps the char as a one-glyph sym.
n 0
col proto sym
col pos num
fn pieceOf {'.'=𝕩 ? "" ; ⋈𝕩}
